The upstream repository is referenced as a git submodule (upstream/goose) and is
not modified. Upstream code copied into this repository lives only under
src/upstream_copy/; each file there names the upstream file, lines and commit it
was taken from, the original work and its license, and what was changed, as
section 4 of the Apache License 2.0 requires. Upstream runtime code restated in
another form (src/wasm/floatfmt.h: upstream's float formatting, as WebAssembly
instructions) carries the same kind of header: the upstream file, functions and
commit it derives from, the original work and its license, and how it was
changed. The goose-wasm executable is built from upstream's compiler sources as
well as this project's.

The executable also includes upstream's vendored cute_spirv
(upstream/goose/third_party/cute_spirv; zlib license or public domain).

The upstream repository bundles third-party code under its own licenses,
including TinyCC (GNU LGPL 2.1, upstream/goose/third_party/tinycc/COPYING).
This project does not copy or redistribute that code.

